      "writtenOn": "2017-01-24T00:48:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking of adding a CMD_DIAGS_CONNECT_TIMEOUT, to catch this, and any other similar cases. The idea is as follows:\n- reportConnectAttemptStart() would use sendMessageDelayed(), to queue up a timeout\n- I\u0027d modify DefaultState to recognize CMD_DIAGS_CONNECT_TIMEOUT, and call reportConnectionEvent(WifiDiagnostics.CONNECTION_EVENT_FAILED).\n- I\u0027d add a connectionId parameter to reportConnectionEvent()\n- I\u0027d LastMileLogger to check that a failure event actually corresponds to the most recent CONNECTION_EVENT_START.\n\nHow\u0027s that sound?\n\nIf that sounds good, I\u0027d like to handle that in a follow-on CL. (Just to keep each CL small and focused.)",
